# Hashed fixtures MUST NOT be line-ending translated.
#
# The TraderX EOD bundles under tests/fixtures/traderx-eod/ are pinned by
# SHA-256 hashes over their exact committed bytes. On a Windows checkout with
# core.autocrlf=true (Git for Windows' installer default), git rewrites
# LF -> CRLF on checkout for anything it considers text -- which includes
# .json and .csv. Every artifact hash then fails, with nothing in the error
# pointing at the cause.
#
# This is not hypothetical. It is exactly what happened to the vendored
# reference/traderX checkout in this repository, and it had already broken
# TraderX's own verifier before that. See engine/integration/bundle.py's
# module docstring and docs/planning/traderx-integration-plan.md §W0.1.
#
# `-text` disables all line-ending translation in both directions, so the
# bytes in the working tree are always the committed bytes.
*.json -text
*.csv  -text
